asr-000064
00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:22.710
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: With your permission, and with the Committee's kind indulgence, allow me to present the

asr-000065
00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:26.850
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: key highlights of our proposed fiscal year 2027 budget and strategic priorities.

asr-000066
00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:33.570
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For a more detailed discussion of these highlights, I respectfully refer the Honorable Members

asr-000067
00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:37.150
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to the printed copies that have been distributed for your reference.

asr-000068
00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:44.010
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: The DENR respectfully requests for a total budget of 28.04 billion pesos.

asr-000069
00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:51.910
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: This amount covers the DENR Central Office, our 17 regional offices, all staff and line bureaus,

asr-000070
00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:54.330
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and attached agencies.

asr-000071
00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:59.870
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: With an immense mandate covering 15.8 million hectares of classified forest lands and over

asr-000072
00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:05.910
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: 36,000 kilometers of coastline, the Department is entrusted with a challenging, yet vital

asr-000073
00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.810
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: responsibility.

asr-000074
00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:12.530
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Our primary priority is translating this mandate into direct community impact.

asr-000075
00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:19.310
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Amid limitations in fiscal space, we commit to channeling our resources toward three highly

asr-000076
00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:20.040
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: impactful pillars.

asr-000081
00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:26.640
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: First, we are unlocking our natural capital to drive sustainable socio-economic development.

asr-000082
00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:32.140
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We are transforming the National Greening Program into a forest landscape restoration

asr-000083
00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:39.270
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: approach focusing on priority landscapes such as the Sierra Madre Protected Landscape.

asr-000084
00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:45.650
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For 2027, we aim to support community-based social enterprises, ensuring that we do not

asr-000085
00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:51.910
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: merely plant trees, but restore biodiversity, strengthen ecosystem resilience, and create

asr-000086
00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.170
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: sustainable livelihoods for local communities.

asr-000087
00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:58.530
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We are aggressively scaling up our land titling program.

asr-000088
00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:05.430
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Our goal is to issue up to 43,000 land patents in 2027, providing absolute tenure security

asr-000089
00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:10.490
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: that unlocks vital economic capital for families and households.

asr-000090
00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:16.440
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: In the mining sector, we are driving towards a 2% mining GDP contribution by 2028.

asr-000091
00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:23.070
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We will maximize our mineral wealth by empowering small-scale miners through the Minahang Bayan Program

asr-000098
00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:27.010
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and fast-tracking critical mineral quadrangle mapping, balanced

asr-000099
00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:31.610
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: strictly with rigorous regulatory compliance monitoring and enforcement.

asr-000100
00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.790
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Second, we are advancing a clean and healthy environment.

asr-000101
00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.770
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Reliable access to clean water is a fundamental right.

asr-000102
00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:47.330
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For 2027, we are providing 124 million pesos in direct financial assistance to local water

asr-000103
00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:47.710
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: districts.

asr-000104
00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:52.130
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to expand services to isolated and unserved barangays.

asr-000106
00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:59.050
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: On solid waste management, we continue to empower the local government units and provide them with technical assistance.

asr-000107
00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:04.330
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Furthermore, our implementation of the Extended Producer Responsibility Act

asr-000108
00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:13.190
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: has already mobilized over 1,000 enterprises, diverting 244 million kilograms of waste packaging footprint.

asr-000109
00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:20.390
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: As part of this effort, we shall aggressively continue our revitalization of major urban waterways,

asr-000110
00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:24.450
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: particularly the Manila Bay, Pasig River system, and Laguna Lake.

asr-000111
00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:29.450
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Third, we are strengthening ecosystem integrity and climate resilience.

asr-000112
00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:37.370
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Through the Mines and Geosciences Bureau, we are operating a 24-7 geohazards operations center that sends direct,

asr-000113
00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:42.630
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: real-time threat advisories to LGUs to protect at-risk barangays.

asr-000114
00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:48.030
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We are specifically targeting our interventions to the 18 high-exposure

asr-000115
00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:53.650
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: provinces identified in the National Adaptation Plan to support risk-informed planning.

asr-000116
00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:59.950
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because ecosystems are our strongest natural defense, we are strengthening the active management

asr-000117
00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:05.930
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: of our 121 legislated protected areas and our marine protected area networks.

asr-000118
00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:32.150
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Fundamental to all these priorities is the paradigm shift brought about by the PENCAS law. The department is currently enhancing its technical capacity and workforce to establish site-specific ecosystem accounts. By measuring the economic value of our environment, the ecosystem services, and the tangible benefits of conservation, we are enabling smarter, data-driven planning, programming, and budgeting.

asr-000119
00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:50.300
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: To conclude, Mr. Chair, Honorable Members of the Committee, financing the environment and natural resources is a strategic investment toward achieving nature-positive, climate-resilient, and sustainable Filipino communities and livelihoods. We seek your support in passing the budget. Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

