asr-001270
01:12:19.822 --> 01:12:22.040
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The problem of flooding.

asr-001271
01:12:24.298 --> 01:12:28.933
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Now, I am here for the deliberation of the DNR.

asr-001272
01:12:28.933 --> 01:12:38.423
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: And last week, I gave a privileged speech and I said myself that the National Solid Waste Commission is inutile.

asr-001273
01:12:39.242 --> 01:12:46.275
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Because this law has been around for 25 years, we are always in Grade 2.

asr-001274
01:12:46.615 --> 01:12:57.264
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: It means that the flooding problem in our society in Metro Manila is not only the problem of the DPWH,

asr-001275
01:12:57.963 --> 01:12:58.882
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: but also the problem of the DPWH.

asr-001276
01:12:58.902 --> 01:13:06.074
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The problem is also the garbage that is being washed in the canals.

asr-001277
01:13:08.442 --> 01:13:12.857
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Now, Mr. Chair, I would like to ask Secretary Cunha,

asr-001278
01:13:13.737 --> 01:13:24.745
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: what are your concrete plans to solve this garbage crisis which floods our nation every time a typhoon hits our country?

asr-001279
01:13:24.745 --> 01:13:30.359
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: As a Commission Chairman of the National Solid Waste Commission,

asr-001280
01:13:30.379 --> 01:13:31.678
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: what are your concrete plans to solve this garbage crisis which floods our nation every time a typhoon hits our country?

asr-001281
01:13:31.678 --> 01:13:39.550
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary, please answer another privileged speech given by Congressman Bong Temes.

asr-001282
01:13:40.389 --> 01:13:41.248
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Kindly answer.

asr-001283
01:13:42.087 --> 01:13:43.366
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001284
01:13:43.745 --> 01:13:51.018
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Actually, solid waste management has been a big issue for the last few weeks,

asr-001285
01:13:51.158 --> 01:13:55.213
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: particularly because of the heavy rains that we have been experiencing throughout the country,

asr-001286
01:13:55.913 --> 01:13:59.349
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and particularly here in the National Capital Region, Mr. Chair.

asr-001287
01:14:00.348 --> 01:14:03.045
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: In fact, just to share with the body,

asr-001288
01:14:04.424 --> 01:14:06.981
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: the Executive Secretary called for a meeting last week,

asr-001289
01:14:07.041 --> 01:14:15.672
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: which I participated in along with MMDA and our other agencies, including DPWH,

asr-001290
01:14:15.672 --> 01:14:19.548
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: which talked about the problem of garbage,

asr-001291
01:14:20.088 --> 01:14:29.838
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: which is a big contributor in terms of the heavy flooding that we have been experiencing lately.

asr-001292
01:14:30.317 --> 01:14:34.393
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: The Commission, Mr. Chair, that you're referring to,

asr-001293
01:14:34.393 --> 01:14:35.592
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: of course, it's a policy.

asr-001294
01:14:36.411 --> 01:14:49.098
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: It was also discussed in the Commission that maybe one of the things that we really need to pursue is our enforcement.

asr-001295
01:14:49.098 --> 01:14:56.400
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because we are always asked when...

asr-001296
01:14:56.680 --> 01:15:02.813
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: pagka meron mga proposals even way back more than 10 years ago,

asr-001297
01:15:02.933 --> 01:15:11.404
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: nung nag-uumpisa pa lamang mag-introduce sa mga LGUs ng ordinances that would ban single-use plastics,

asr-001298
01:15:11.544 --> 01:15:13.862
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: kung anong opinion po natin in the DNR.

asr-001299
01:15:14.361 --> 01:15:17.278
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And yung sinasagot po natin is that,

asr-001300
01:15:18.097 --> 01:15:24.990
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: siyempre we support anything that would lessen any type of solid waste in circulation,

asr-001301
01:15:24.990 --> 01:15:30.840
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: pero palagay ko po ang mahalaga ay yung tamang pagtatapon lang po.

asr-001302
01:15:30.840 --> 01:15:39.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So the proper waste disposal is the root cause of the contribution of solid waste dun sa flooding po natin.

asr-001303
01:15:40.020 --> 01:15:46.700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So enforcement, in fact, napag-usapan po namin nila SILG at MMDA last week

asr-001304
01:15:46.700 --> 01:15:53.720
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: when the President was called for a briefing on the situation dito sa Metro Manila

asr-001305
01:15:53.720 --> 01:15:55.580
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: regarding solid waste disposal.

asr-001306
01:15:55.820 --> 01:16:01.960
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: At I think it's high time na magkaroon po tayo ng honest-to-goodness enforcement also,

asr-001307
01:16:03.530 --> 01:16:08.086
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: not just the LGUs, pati po kami at DILG,

asr-001308
01:16:08.665 --> 01:16:13.460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to ensure that the different local government units, particularly the barangay,

asr-001309
01:16:13.680 --> 01:16:21.072
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: take care of their areas of jurisdiction and ensure that proper solid waste management is observed.

asr-001310
01:16:21.072 --> 01:16:24.329
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Dahil ito pong nagiging problema talaga natin kung,

asr-001311
01:16:24.928 --> 01:16:30.003
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: at ano pang material po ang pinag-uusapan natin, whether it's plastics, whether it's anything else,

asr-001312
01:16:30.303 --> 01:16:35.098
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: if it's properly disposed of, we would not be experiencing what we are experiencing now, Mr. Chair.

asr-001313
01:16:35.577 --> 01:16:44.728
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, to your point, Mr. Chair, maybe the Commission needs to come up with better, more concrete policies

asr-001314
01:16:44.728 --> 01:16:51.580
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to ensure enforcement, the proper use of the materials recovery facilities,

asr-001315
01:16:51.580 --> 01:16:54.697
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: which are mandated by the law.

asr-001316
01:16:54.897 --> 01:17:01.330
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Which, admittedly, hindi pa po fully compliant lahat ng 42,000 barangays.

asr-001317
01:17:01.810 --> 01:17:08.503
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Meron pa rin po pagkukulang, or meron pong mga nakatayong mga MRF in certain LGUs,

asr-001318
01:17:08.583 --> 01:17:11.000
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: but which are not actually properly used.

asr-001319
01:17:11.740 --> 01:17:15.835
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Para lang for compliance sake, meron po silang nakatayong MRF.

asr-001320
01:17:15.835 --> 01:17:23.647
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And, of course, napapag-usapan lately po ang possible use of technology,

asr-001321
01:17:24.866 --> 01:17:27.683
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to address yung solid waste management problem po, Mr. Chair.

asr-001322
01:17:28.662 --> 01:17:29.641
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Congressman Teves?

asr-001323
01:17:30.380 --> 01:17:41.928
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Mr. Chair, based sa inyong NIP, mayroong 92% compliance ng mga LGUs sa Ecological Solid Waste Management Act.

asr-001324
01:17:42.707 --> 01:17:48.202
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: At may target kayong gawing 95% ito sa year 2027.

asr-001325
01:17:48.202 --> 01:17:53.576
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Ibig sabihin, kung titingnan natin, is almost 100% neto.

asr-001326
01:17:53.676 --> 01:17:54.815
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: 92% neto.

asr-001327
01:17:54.835 --> 01:17:58.471
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Pero ang tanong, bakit sobra pa rin ang baha?

asr-001328
01:17:58.831 --> 01:18:04.964
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: And then, based sa Solid Waste Management Monitoring of the MMDA,

asr-001329
01:18:06.083 --> 01:18:20.288
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: only 6 out of 17 LGUs in Metro Manila are compliant with the segregation at source mandated by Republic Act 9003.

asr-001330
01:18:20.288 --> 01:18:24.284
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: What is the DENR doing to ensure that the others...

asr-001331
01:18:24.804 --> 01:18:27.361
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: 11 LGUs will be compliant?

asr-001332
01:18:27.921 --> 01:18:35.692
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Before the Secretary answers, let me just acknowledge the House of Representatives to the Commission on Appointments,

asr-001333
01:18:36.272 --> 01:18:38.250
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the Honorable Tony Pett Albano.

asr-001334
01:18:38.669 --> 01:18:41.646
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please reply now.

asr-001335
01:18:42.825 --> 01:18:47.001
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-001336
01:18:47.141 --> 01:18:49.658
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Before I defer to the Environmental Management Bureau,

asr-001337
01:18:49.658 --> 01:18:55.652
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: I think, if I'm not mistaken, that 92% compliance,

asr-001338
01:18:56.371 --> 01:19:01.306
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: was pertaining to submission of Solid Waste Management Plans, Mr. Chair.

asr-001339
01:19:01.306 --> 01:19:14.592
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, meron pong provision under RA 9003, which requires all the local government units to submit 10-year Solid Waste Management Plans.

asr-001340
01:19:15.012 --> 01:19:19.827
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, the law was signed way back in 2001.

asr-001341
01:19:21.185 --> 01:19:26.280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, ngayon po, 92% na po ang nakapag-submit ng Solid Waste Management Plans.

asr-001342
01:19:26.340 --> 01:19:31.455
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But the challenge is the implementation of these plans that have been submitted.

asr-001343
01:19:31.994 --> 01:19:42.703
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: I'd like to defer, Mr. Chair, with the kind indulgence of the Committee to Atty. Matias of the EMB to provide more information, Mr. Chair.

asr-001344
01:19:43.242 --> 01:19:44.941
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Atty. Matias is recognized.

asr-001345
01:19:45.860 --> 01:19:47.078
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001346
01:19:47.638 --> 01:19:51.434
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: For Solid Waste Management, sir, tama po na.

asr-001347
01:19:51.953 --> 01:19:56.029
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: It's 92%, but as said by the Secretary, the Honorable Secretary,

asr-001348
01:19:56.309 --> 01:19:59.126
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: it's only insofar as the approval of the plans.

asr-001349
01:20:00.085 --> 01:20:02.622
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: Na-approve po ito ng Solid Waste Management Commission,

asr-001350
01:20:02.842 --> 01:20:12.232
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: and ang focus po natin right now would be to monitor their compliance insofar as the plan approved by the Solid Waste Management Commission.

asr-001351
01:20:12.552 --> 01:20:20.783
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: And supposed to be po, I mean, the plan should include, sir, yung segregation at source, segregated collection,

asr-001352
01:20:20.783 --> 01:20:23.441
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: and as mandated po by law,

asr-001353
01:20:23.920 --> 01:20:26.238
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: ang dapat pong napupunta sa ating,

asr-001354
01:20:26.278 --> 01:20:28.975
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: yung mga sanitary landfills ay residual waste lang po.

asr-001355
01:20:29.375 --> 01:20:31.293
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: Kaya po, kung mapapansin po natin,

asr-001356
01:20:31.652 --> 01:20:34.549
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: mixed waste po yung mga nasa sanitary landfills,

asr-001357
01:20:34.669 --> 01:20:36.767
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: kaya medyo mabilis po siyang mapuno,

asr-001358
01:20:36.967 --> 01:20:40.023
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: and nakakaroon po ng problema, kinalaunan.

asr-001359
01:20:40.123 --> 01:20:45.098
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: That's why, as part of the instruction to us by the Secretary,

asr-001360
01:20:45.758 --> 01:20:50.153
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: we will now also be focusing on compliance by establishments,

asr-001361
01:20:50.453 --> 01:20:51.780
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: pagdating po sa segregation at source,

asr-001362
01:20:51.780 --> 01:20:56.380
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: and at the same time, we will likewise be monitoring yung segregation,

asr-001365
01:20:56.380 --> 01:20:59.360
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: leading to the sanitary landfills po,

asr-001366
01:20:59.943 --> 01:21:06.536
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: to make sure that yung mapupunta lang po sa sanitary landfills ay mga residual waste.

asr-001367
01:21:06.656 --> 01:21:11.291
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: But aminado po tayo that we will have to work with different stakeholders po,

asr-001368
01:21:11.391 --> 01:21:13.948
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: and other government agencies like the DILG,

asr-001369
01:21:14.288 --> 01:21:17.604
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: to achieve po yung objective natin of segregated collection po.

asr-001370
01:21:20.132 --> 01:21:20.711
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Mr. Chair?

asr-001371
01:21:21.011 --> 01:21:22.809
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please proceed, Congressman Tevez.

asr-001372
01:21:24.088 --> 01:21:26.665
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Ito ba ay paper compliance?

asr-001373
01:21:26.865 --> 01:21:27.804
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Paano nyo ito namamunin?

asr-001374
01:21:28.164 --> 01:21:32.239
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please answer, Attorney Matias.

asr-001375
01:21:32.539 --> 01:21:32.998
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: Yes, sir.

asr-001376
01:21:33.138 --> 01:21:37.514
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: The department issued an instruction to the regional offices

asr-001377
01:21:37.514 --> 01:21:43.807
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: requiring the targets of compliance ng mga establishments po natin

asr-001378
01:21:43.807 --> 01:21:45.665
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: insofar as segregation at source,

asr-001379
01:21:46.205 --> 01:21:50.600
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: and likewise look into the segregated collection.

asr-001380
01:21:51.200 --> 01:21:52.898
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: Pagdating po dito sa mga waste,

asr-001381
01:21:53.038 --> 01:21:55.016
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: kasi ang experience po natin,

asr-001382
01:21:55.016 --> 01:21:58.013
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: although some establishments are practicing segregation,

asr-001383
01:21:58.132 --> 01:21:59.191
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: segregation at source,

asr-001384
01:21:59.631 --> 01:22:02.028
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: pero yung collection po, magkakasama pa rin po.

asr-001385
01:22:02.288 --> 01:22:05.285
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: And ito po yung binabantayan po natin.

asr-001386
01:22:05.405 --> 01:22:12.378
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: And corresponding notices will be issued to those involved in the activity, sir.

asr-001387
01:22:13.596 --> 01:22:15.335
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you. Congressman Tevez?

asr-001388
01:22:15.754 --> 01:22:21.069
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Mr. Chair, may partner ba kayo sa sinasabing yung segregation at source?

asr-001389
01:22:21.069 --> 01:22:27.062
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Kasi tinuturoan nyo na mag-segregate ang household basis sa

asr-001390
01:22:28.101 --> 01:22:30.519
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: sa Republic Act 9003.

asr-001391
01:22:31.358 --> 01:22:38.630
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: But ang tanong ko, may partner ba kayo para humakot sa inyo ng recyclables?

asr-001392
01:22:39.470 --> 01:22:44.185
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Siguro pwedeng sumagot sa akin ng taga National Solid Waste Commission o taga ENB.

asr-001393
01:22:44.784 --> 01:22:47.062
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Kasi wala akong nakikitang partners nyo.

asr-001394
01:22:49.729 --> 01:22:51.087
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Anong nangyayari, Mr. Chair?

asr-001395
01:22:51.787 --> 01:22:54.364
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Turo sila ng turo kung paano mag-segregate.

asr-001396
01:22:54.744 --> 01:22:59.778
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: After nilang maturo, wala silang ipakikilala kung sino ang hahakot ng recyclables.

asr-001399
01:23:05.075 --> 01:23:08.028
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you. You have 35 seconds more.

asr-001400
01:23:08.028 --> 01:23:12.560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair. I'd like to defer to Usec. Rodriguez who chairs the commission.

asr-001401
01:23:13.411 --> 01:23:14.879
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Good morning, po.

asr-001402
01:23:15.600 --> 01:23:20.740
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Sir, I'd like to answer first your previous question regarding the National Solid Waste Management Commission.

asr-001403
01:23:21.120 --> 01:23:24.840
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So it is correct that it actually is under the office of the President.

asr-001404
01:23:24.840 --> 01:23:28.080
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: And it is chaired by the DENR.

asr-001405
01:23:28.080 --> 01:23:31.740
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: But the way that the commission...

asr-001406
01:23:31.740 --> 01:23:34.980
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: The commission was set up, actually, even 25 years ago,

asr-001407
01:23:35.240 --> 01:23:38.380
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: yung members po niya, whole of society approached na.

asr-001408
01:23:38.480 --> 01:23:42.160
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: We have various government agencies represented.

asr-001409
01:23:42.760 --> 01:23:46.060
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Meron pong tatlong NGO kasama po doon ng eco-waste.

asr-001410
01:23:46.160 --> 01:23:47.800
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: At kasama po ang private sector.

asr-001411
01:23:48.020 --> 01:23:52.380
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Nakasama pong mga nasa packaging at mga ibang-ibang mga ano, no?

asr-001412
01:23:52.380 --> 01:23:53.820
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Na nag-generate po ng solid waste.

asr-001413
01:23:53.820 --> 01:23:58.620
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ang budget po ng National Solid Waste Management Commission is zero.

asr-001414
01:23:59.540 --> 01:24:00.740
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Okay, wala po siyang budget.

asr-001415
01:24:01.120 --> 01:24:02.840
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Nakukuha lang po siya sa EMB.

asr-001416
01:24:02.920 --> 01:24:07.280
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Under 9003, EMB will act as a secretariat.

asr-001417
01:24:07.460 --> 01:24:14.620
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ang nakukuha lang pong budget ng National Solid Waste Commission from the EMB is only around 3.5 million pesos a year.

asr-001418
01:24:15.880 --> 01:24:18.540
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, ngayon po, wala pong staffing ang commission.

asr-001419
01:24:18.540 --> 01:24:23.500
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: At the same time, ang nangyayari po, no?

asr-001420
01:24:23.500 --> 01:24:31.960
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: I think it was mentioned that out of the 1,592 LGUs who are supposed to submit their 10-year solid waste management,

asr-001421
01:24:32.180 --> 01:24:37.220
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: only 92% is 1,460.

asr-001422
01:24:37.220 --> 01:24:47.600
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ang ginagawa po ng commission is sila po dapat ang nag-check kung sumusunod po ang mga LGU sa mga kanilang mga plano.

asr-001423
01:24:48.140 --> 01:24:52.840
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Pero since wala pong tao ang commission, ang mga commissioners po mismo ang umiikot.

asr-001424
01:24:52.960 --> 01:24:58.100
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: At ang naiikutan lang po dila, if I'm not mistaken, every year is around 12 to 20.

asr-001425
01:24:58.280 --> 01:24:59.980
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, I think that also is one of the reasons.

asr-001426
01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:01.560
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Now, to answer.

