asr-003257
02:50:39.760 --> 02:50:41.940
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: On the first question, Mr. Chair, as we know,

asr-003258
02:50:45.080 --> 02:50:50.060
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: there is an existing prohibition on the cutting of mangroves.

asr-003259
02:50:50.820 --> 02:50:51.260
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Yes. Yes.

asr-003261
02:50:52.460 --> 02:51:02.420
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, the method that is allowed is to earthball the mangroves.

asr-003262
02:51:04.860 --> 02:51:22.660
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Right now, as mentioned earlier, Mr. Chair, the central office led by Yusek Mark Fragada and Yusek Ernesto Adobo, Jr. had a meeting with the staff of the good congresswoman, Mr. Chair,

asr-003265
02:51:22.660 --> 02:51:44.660
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and we explained the fact that this memo is an offshoot of many requests because at that time, there was a suspension on the issuance of earthball. There was a suspension on the issuance of earthball permits issued by the Biodiversity Management Bureau at that time.

asr-003268
02:51:44.660 --> 02:51:54.660
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But this took quite a while with no clear end in sight at that time.

asr-003269
02:51:55.440 --> 02:52:06.340
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And there were so many requests for government projects for earthballing permits for the project to continue.

asr-003271
02:52:06.340 --> 02:52:12.140
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Just to clarify, inform the body, Mr. Chair,

asr-003273
02:52:12.140 --> 02:52:19.780
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: that in the DNR, we follow the hierarchy of mitigation for proposed projects.

asr-003274
02:52:20.580 --> 02:52:25.920
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: First, number one is avoidance.

asr-003275
02:52:26.160 --> 02:52:31.780
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: If we can avoid cutting anything, trees, mangroves, anything,

asr-003276
02:52:35.480 --> 02:52:36.400
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: that is a choice that we will make.

asr-003277
02:52:36.580 --> 02:52:38.720
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But if this is not possible,

asr-003278
02:52:38.720 --> 02:52:44.540
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: due to whatever reason, the design or the project proposal,

asr-003279
02:52:45.220 --> 02:52:47.600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: then we have minimization.

asr-003280
02:52:47.920 --> 02:52:55.740
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So the least number that we need to cut or to earthball, then that is what we will do.

asr-003282
02:52:55.820 --> 02:53:00.960
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Then the third is rehabilitation or restoration, Mr. Chair.

asr-003283
02:53:00.960 --> 02:53:02.740
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And the last is offsetting.

asr-003284
02:53:03.540 --> 02:53:08.960
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So this is an internationally recognized hierarchy of mitigation.

asr-003285
02:53:08.960 --> 02:53:10.840
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: That is, faith, Инformation, provisions that are used worldwide.

asr-003289
02:53:12.880 --> 02:53:15.200
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, going back, Mr. Chair,

asr-003290
02:53:15.360 --> 02:53:18.700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: we had many requests from the DOTR and DPWH,

asr-003291
02:53:22.180 --> 02:53:24.700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and other government agencies and even private entities for earthballing.

asr-003292
02:53:27.180 --> 02:53:28.060
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So,

asr-003293
02:53:28.060 --> 02:53:31.000
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: as Undersecretary for Field Operations,

asr-003294
02:53:32.160 --> 02:54:02.540
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We sat down with the Ecosystems Research and Development Bureau, which is our research arm, ERDB, of course, along with BNB, the Biodiversity Management Bureau, and we requested them to come up with a study on the earth boiling of mangroves, particularly on the survival rate, Mr. Chair.

asr-003295
02:54:02.540 --> 02:54:09.460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And the first phase was already completed, and the second phase is ongoing.

asr-003296
02:54:16.900 --> 02:54:22.360
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because the study is differing with regard to the size of the mangroves that are undergoing the study, Mr. Chair.

asr-003297
02:54:22.780 --> 02:54:27.840
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, right now, the second phase of the study is approaching.

asr-003298
02:54:30.100 --> 02:54:34.240
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: It is projected to be completed by December of this year, Mr. Chair.

asr-003299
02:54:37.900 --> 02:54:44.220
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And with the result of that study, we will be coming up with a policy in the early part of 2027.

asr-003300
02:54:44.220 --> 02:55:04.220
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Now, we have created a technical working group to work on this policy moving forward, and we have included members of civil society, Mr. Chair, along with the DNR, the Ecosystems Research and Development Bureau.

asr-003301
02:55:05.260 --> 02:55:27.340
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: The Development Bureau, ERDB, and BNB, and also members of civil society, particularly WWF, the World Wildlife Fund, and the Forest Foundation of the Philippines, and two more NGOs, Mr. Chair.

asr-003302
02:55:27.840 --> 02:55:29.840
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, that is where we are right now, Mr. Chair.

asr-003303
