Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Dahil this is just a reminder. The extraction of natural resources is only reserved for Filipino citizens.

asr-003320
02:56:13.260 --> 02:56:17.820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: You didn't just change your registration, you gave them a permit immediately.

asr-003321
02:56:19.280 --> 02:56:20.420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-003322
02:56:22.820 --> 02:56:28.420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: May we have, because Congressman Rufus Rodriguez would like to see the list of the bona fide mining operators.

asr-003323
02:56:28.420 --> 02:56:33.260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: We are very, very... We are very concerned about this, Mr. Secretary.

asr-003325
02:56:35.320 --> 02:56:36.580
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-003326
02:56:36.660 --> 02:56:41.020
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, we will submit a full report both to the committee and to the good congresswoman.

asr-003327
02:56:41.380 --> 02:56:42.160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yes, please. Mr. Chair.

asr-003329
02:56:43.180 --> 02:56:51.600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: On number three, Mr. Chair, if I may defer to Director Larry Herades of the Mines and Geosciences Bureau.

asr-003331
02:56:51.740 --> 02:56:53.280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: This is regarding the FTAAs.

asr-003332
02:56:54.020 --> 02:56:54.900
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Larry, you have the floor.

asr-003333
02:56:54.900 --> 02:56:56.100
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Mr. Chair,

asr-003334
02:56:56.220 --> 02:57:01.380
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: currently we have six FTAAs approved by the President of the Philippines.

asr-003335
02:57:01.700 --> 02:57:03.240
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Dalawa po yung nag-ooperate.

asr-003336
02:57:03.320 --> 02:57:07.700
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: One is in Nueva Vizcaya, in Oceana Gold.

asr-003337
02:57:08.310 --> 02:57:13.100
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: And another one also in Nueva Vizcaya is the FCF.

asr-003338
02:57:16.180 --> 02:57:23.880
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Both are operating for Golden Copper. There are four FTAAs under exploration period.

asr-003340
02:57:24.900 --> 02:57:28.220
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: In Mindoro, in South Cotabado, which is Tampacan.

asr-003341
02:57:29.240 --> 02:57:31.140
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Mindoro?

asr-003342
02:57:31.280 --> 02:57:32.840
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Mindoro. Mindoro?

asr-003344
02:57:32.900 --> 02:57:34.880
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Mindoro. There is no mining there.

asr-003346
02:57:34.880 --> 02:57:37.220
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Yes, that is why they are not operating.

asr-003347
02:57:37.220 --> 02:57:38.860
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: There is no exploration. You are right.

asr-003349
02:57:39.540 --> 02:57:40.560
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: I know they are fighting when they are mining there. Yes.

asr-003351
02:57:40.760 --> 02:57:44.740
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Another one is in the area of Pangasinan La Union, which is a mix of offshore and onshore

asr-003352
02:57:45.260 --> 02:57:46.860
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: areas.

asr-003353
02:57:46.860 --> 02:57:48.840
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Also not operating.

asr-003354
02:57:50.140 --> 02:57:52.180
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Another one is in Palawan, which was cancelled, but under a court litigation in Palawan.

asr-003355
02:57:52.180 --> 02:57:58.000
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Those are the four non-operating.

asr-003356
02:57:59.220 --> 02:58:04.140
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: All in all, we have six FTAAs.

asr-003357
02:58:04.700 --> 02:58:12.080
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: In the question of renewal of Tampacan, all of our FTAA contracts, there is a provision

asr-003358
02:58:14.400 --> 02:58:23.660
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: that if a suspension is attributable to force majeure, they can enjoy the period of non-operation

asr-003359
02:58:23.660 --> 02:58:26.880
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: because of force majeure and we can extend it.

asr-003360
02:58:26.880 --> 02:58:29.800
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: There are instances like that.

asr-003366
02:58:29.800 --> 02:58:44.600
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Contractors are availing of that provision that has been approved by the DNR and even the President of the Philippines when it comes to the FTAAs. That is the status of the FTAA.

asr-003369
02:58:44.600 --> 02:58:45.140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Okay.

asr-003370
02:58:45.920 --> 02:58:46.800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: So, number three?

asr-003371
02:58:49.520 --> 02:58:50.820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Four, Mr. Chair, if I may.

asr-003372
02:58:51.180 --> 02:58:51.920
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Number four?

asr-003373
02:58:52.120 --> 02:58:52.840
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Number four. Yeah.

asr-003375
02:58:52.900 --> 02:59:07.100
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For the details on Zambales China Harbor in particular, may I defer to the Regional Director? The Director of MGB, R.D. Glenn Noble, Mr. Chair, of Region 3.

asr-003378
02:59:07.160 --> 02:59:07.560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Where is Glenn?

asr-003379
02:59:08.400 --> 02:59:11.680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Glenn, you find a microphone and speak louder.

asr-003380
02:59:11.860 --> 02:59:12.440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yes, sir, Mr. Chair.

asr-003381
02:59:12.440 --> 02:59:13.220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Everybody can hear you.

asr-003382
02:59:13.400 --> 02:59:13.820
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Yes, sir.

asr-003383
02:59:14.160 --> 02:59:15.340
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Good afternoon.

asr-003384
02:59:15.340 --> 02:59:18.900
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Good afternoon to everyone in this body.

asr-003385
02:59:19.160 --> 02:59:20.940
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Thank you very much for your question.

asr-003386
02:59:21.040 --> 02:59:28.340
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Mr. Chair, there is no such thing as, there is no company as mentioned by our good congressman

asr-003387
02:59:28.890 --> 02:59:31.300
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: about a certain China dredging company.

asr-003388
02:59:32.260 --> 02:59:33.160
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: That is why.

asr-003389
02:59:34.540 --> 02:59:36.160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It used to exist.

asr-003390
02:59:37.000 --> 02:59:40.720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It used to exist.

asr-003391
02:59:41.560 --> 02:59:42.540
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It doesn't exist anymore. Don't say what Congresswoman Lima is saying.

asr-003393
02:59:42.700 --> 02:59:44.360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It doesn't exist.

asr-003394
02:59:44.540 --> 02:59:45.260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It used to exist.

asr-003395
02:59:46.460 --> 02:59:53.860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Maybe, Mr. Chair. You don't know.

asr-003397
02:59:53.980 --> 02:59:55.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: No, Mr. Chair, just to clarify, R.D. Glenn Noble has just assumed... It's just assumed Region 3, maybe three weeks ago, bago lang siya.

asr-003399
02:59:55.320 --> 02:59:59.860
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Nag-retire na, mandatory retirement yung RD doon eh.

asr-003400
02:59:59.860 --> 03:00:01.760
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Better consult with Governor Ibrani.

asr-003401
03:00:02.660 --> 03:00:11.000
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Right now po, Mr. Chair, the operators in the three rivers, Maloma River, Santo Tomas River, Bukaw River, are as follows.

asr-003402
03:00:11.320 --> 03:00:14.080
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: In Maloma River po, it's Halray Construction.

asr-003403
03:00:14.960 --> 03:00:18.400
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: In Santo Tomas River po, it's Shelfood Resources Incorporated.

asr-003404
03:00:18.720 --> 03:00:21.340
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: In Bukaw River po, ito po yung may lima.

asr-003405
03:00:21.620 --> 03:00:23.820
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Greenfield Mineral Exploration and Development Corp.

asr-003406
03:00:24.040 --> 03:00:27.520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saan daw dinadala lahat ng buhangin na yan? Sabi ni Congresswoman.

asr-003407
03:00:27.880 --> 03:00:33.360
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Sa atin pong recla... ah, sa may, what's this, sa may Bulacan po, sa may airport po.

asr-003408
03:00:33.580 --> 03:00:37.000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ah, doon sa new airport ni San Miguel?

asr-003409
03:00:37.260 --> 03:00:37.820
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Yes, po.

asr-003410
03:00:37.820 --> 03:00:40.560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi dito sa reklamasyon ng dalawa? Hindi?

asr-003411
03:00:43.500 --> 03:00:45.400
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Pati po lang sa may Manila Bay.

asr-003412
03:00:45.400 --> 03:00:48.780
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ah, kayo pala yung nagtatambak dyan sa Manila Bay.

asr-003413
03:00:49.040 --> 03:00:49.520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Bulacan Airport.

asr-003414
03:00:49.740 --> 03:00:53.020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Bantay kayo. Bantay kayo dahil si Congresswoman marami pong kasagutan niya.

asr-003416
03:00:53.020 --> 03:00:54.000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sa kutin niyo mabuti.

asr-003419
03:00:54.000 --> 03:01:01.160
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: So, Magna Corp po is another one that's operating in Bukaw River.

asr-003420
03:01:01.160 --> 03:01:07.120
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Seven West Incorporated, Say 2K

asr-003417
03:01:04.160 --> 03:01:04.280
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: Resources Incorporated,

asr-003418
03:01:04.480 --> 03:01:05.360
MGB Region III Regional Director Glenn Marcelo C. Noble: and Chosen One Land Development Corporation po.

asr-003421
03:01:07.120 --> 03:01:09.900
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Chosen One. Grabe ng pangalan.

asr-003422
03:01:09.900 --> 03:01:11.760
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Congresswoman De Lima, are you satisfied?

asr-003423
03:01:12.160 --> 03:01:15.900
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Please, I give you some time to go on ask more question.

asr-003424
03:01:16.540 --> 03:01:17.720
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Your Honors, partially, Mr. Chair.

asr-003425
03:01:17.980 --> 03:01:19.540
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: With respect to the...

asr-003426
03:01:19.540 --> 03:01:21.220
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Earthballing.

asr-003427
03:01:21.980 --> 03:01:27.920
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yes, we understood now that there's a TWG, but I think this is recently created.

asr-003428
03:01:28.160 --> 03:01:29.420
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Just recently created.

asr-003429
03:01:29.700 --> 03:01:39.500
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So, I'm wondering why that memorandum was issued at all, even before consultations or even before TWG or scientific study.

asr-003430
03:01:39.900 --> 03:01:44.600
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Kasi yung survival rate po ata, that's something that is still put into question.

asr-003431
03:01:45.460 --> 03:01:47.440
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: What exactly is the survival rate?

asr-003432
03:01:47.700 --> 03:01:48.420
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Di ho ba?

asr-003433
03:01:48.540 --> 03:01:50.140
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So, all of these things should have been...

asr-003434
03:01:50.140 --> 03:01:55.480
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: confirmed first or verified first before allowing the issuance of this memorandum.

asr-003435
03:01:55.660 --> 03:02:05.280
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yes, it is considered interim operational guidance, but is it really interim or is it a de facto permanent policy na po ngayon?

asr-003436
03:02:05.280 --> 03:02:13.400
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yung pag-a-allow ng, you know, earthballing for the flagship infrastructure?

asr-003437
03:02:13.600 --> 03:02:14.300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Very briefly.

asr-003438
03:02:14.560 --> 03:02:16.500
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Mr. Chair, if I may?

asr-003440
03:02:17.720 --> 03:02:25.400
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Actually, as I said earlier, there were a lot of requests for government projects.

asr-003442
03:02:25.400 --> 03:02:38.900
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And

asr-003439
03:02:26.240 --> 03:02:26.440
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: we deemed it appropriate at the time under the sustainable development that we are following.

asr-003443
03:02:50.740 --> 03:02:53.960
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: To come up with this interim memorandum or interim guidelines through a memorandum,

asr-003444
03:02:54.760 --> 03:03:00.200
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: specifying certain methods or guidelines that had to be followed after consultation with the ERDB,

asr-003445
03:03:00.200 --> 03:03:05.940
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: the Ecosystems Research and Development Bureau, the BMB, and even the Forest Management Bureau.

asr-003446
03:03:08.080 --> 03:03:13.180
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Kasi based on the reports of our technical personnel,

asr-003447
03:03:15.320 --> 03:03:16.640
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: bumaba ba ang survival rate ng...

asr-003448
03:03:16.640 --> 03:03:24.800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: earthballing for several reasons, for several factors.

asr-003449
03:03:25.080 --> 03:03:32.460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: One is, minamadali yung project. So, basta tinatanggal na lang.

asr-003451
03:03:32.580 --> 03:03:44.240
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: It takes time and there's a particular method that should be used in extracting these plants to be transferred,

asr-003452
03:03:44.240 --> 03:03:46.680
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: these trees to be transferred. That's one.

asr-003454
03:03:46.820 --> 03:03:51.640
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Secondly, yung site... identification is another factor.

asr-003456
03:03:51.960 --> 03:04:02.700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, kailangan maghanap talaga ng area where these earthballed trees are transferred.

asr-003457
03:04:02.960 --> 03:04:08.040
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For instance, meron po kaming case in point in the city of Manila.

asr-003458
03:04:08.040 --> 03:04:17.080
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Merong na earthball po na ilang puno doon inilipat sa malapit sa post office.

asr-003459
03:04:17.080 --> 03:04:23.520
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And we have... We have already seen na tumubo na po sa... It grew already from the time...

asr-003462
03:04:23.520 --> 03:04:24.800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: That is not mangrove.

asr-003464
03:04:24.800 --> 03:04:31.400
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Pero ibig sabihin, in terms of... It's another... Earthballing lang po. Yeah, earthballing in general.

asr-003468
03:04:33.160 --> 03:04:40.040
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, actually, we're encouraged by the initial results that have been sent to us already.

asr-003469
03:04:40.220 --> 03:04:50.380
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But for us to be able to really extensively complete the study, we are targeting December of this year, Mr. Chair.

asr-003472
03:04:51.540 --> 03:05:00.760
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Thank you for that. But I'm not very sure about the encouraging results of the study. I think we have to be more... DNR has to be more forthright about that.

asr-003476
03:05:01.400 --> 03:05:04.420
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: The results of the scientific study on the earthballing and survival rate,

asr-003477
03:05:05.820 --> 03:05:06.900
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: masyado atang mababa.

asr-003478
03:05:07.900 --> 03:05:09.880
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Kung hindi man zero percent, I know...

asr-003479
03:05:11.080 --> 03:05:15.100
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Kasi, umang Dilima, would you want to get some advice from an expert from the chair?

asr-003480
03:05:15.740 --> 03:05:16.520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sure, sir.

asr-003481
03:05:16.760 --> 03:05:18.720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Okay, Mr. DNR, Secretary.

asr-003482
03:05:19.680 --> 03:05:21.000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-003483
03:05:21.000 --> 03:05:25.580
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: As far as mangrove is concerned, no need to ball earth.

asr-003484
03:05:26.000 --> 03:05:27.300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Please listen to me.

asr-003485
03:05:28.020 --> 03:05:32.620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: In Malaysia, mangroves are allowed to be cut and utilized.

asr-003486
03:05:33.420 --> 03:05:36.680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Instead of earthballing the mangrove, which is hastily done,

asr-003487
03:05:36.840 --> 03:05:39.820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: and I have not seen a good survival rate,

asr-003488
03:05:40.100 --> 03:05:43.660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: if it is land-based, acacia or manga,

asr-003489
03:05:43.960 --> 03:05:46.160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: yan, madali po nating earthball.

asr-003490
03:05:46.480 --> 03:05:47.360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Bubuhay yan.

asr-003491
03:05:47.520 --> 03:05:49.700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pero mangrove, mahirap po buhayin.

asr-003493
03:05:50.260 --> 03:05:53.560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Instead, ipinalize mo na lang yung Bureau of Concern

asr-003494
03:05:53.560 --> 03:05:56.120
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: or yung private individual, private contractor,

asr-003495
03:05:56.560 --> 03:05:59.760
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: pabayarin mo in order to, kalimbawa,

asr-003496
03:06:00.000 --> 03:06:06.660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: 1,000 square meters yung ma-affected na earthball mo na mangrove,

asr-003497
03:06:06.820 --> 03:06:11.820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: you penalize them for a 1-hectare plantation ng mangrove,

asr-003498
03:06:11.880 --> 03:06:12.900
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: pabayarin mo sila,

asr-003499
03:06:12.900 --> 03:06:14.800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: and that is more effective rather than earthballing 1,000.

asr-003500
03:06:16.060 --> 03:06:17.000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: That's my advice.

asr-003501
03:06:17.180 --> 03:06:19.160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I know very well because I'm a forester.

asr-003502
03:06:19.560 --> 03:06:23.520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Thank you, Madam Representative de Lima,

asr-003503
03:06:23.580 --> 03:06:24.420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: and thank you, Secretary.

asr-003504
03:06:24.820 --> 03:06:28.100
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair, for that suggestion.

asr-003505
03:06:28.100 --> 03:06:39.600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But in this particular instance, Mr. Chair, we are constrained by the fact that it is a law that prohibits the cutting.

asr-003507
03:06:40.980 --> 03:06:48.460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So that's where we are. We need to address it through legislation if we are to allow the cutting of mangroves moving forward. But anyway,

asr-003511
03:06:48.460 --> 03:06:58.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: over and above that, as I mentioned earlier in the hierarchy of mitigation, talagang required naman sila mag-offset. Even if we allow the earthballing,

asr-003515
03:06:58.900 --> 03:07:08.560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: they are required to provide offsetting.

asr-003516
03:07:08.600 --> 03:07:11.420
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So magpa-plant po talaga sila ng mangroves.

asr-003517
03:07:13.320 --> 03:07:14.720
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So that's in the guidelines.

asr-003518
03:07:15.100 --> 03:07:16.020
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Is that in the guidelines?

asr-003519
03:07:16.680 --> 03:07:17.740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: But again, I think,

asr-003520
03:07:19.660 --> 03:07:20.140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: momentarily, Your Honors,

asr-003521
03:07:20.680 --> 03:07:23.320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I wish to suggest that to suspend first the implementation,

asr-003522
03:07:23.860 --> 03:07:25.380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: if not altogether, do away.

asr-003523
03:07:25.380 --> 03:07:27.860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: There's a request to suspend first earthballing on mangroves.

asr-003524
03:07:27.860 --> 03:07:29.760
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mr. Secretary,

asr-003525
03:07:30.500 --> 03:07:31.680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: what say you?

asr-003526
03:07:32.740 --> 03:07:34.880
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Mr. Chair,

asr-003527
03:07:35.420 --> 03:07:37.880
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: with all due respect to the good Congresswoman,

asr-003528
03:07:38.460 --> 03:07:39.460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: we will evaluate that suggestion.

asr-003529
03:07:40.520 --> 03:07:41.640
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But as you know,

asr-003530
03:07:41.880 --> 03:07:45.500
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: there are a lot of developments that are ongoing,

asr-003531
03:07:45.800 --> 03:07:48.020
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: so we need to be able to also balance.

asr-003532
03:07:48.020 --> 03:07:49.960
