Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: This is about your regulation.

asr-005083
04:09:38.660 --> 04:09:58.860
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: You know, the central office is the final approving authority as of now. But before, there was this department, administrative order, which prescribed the processing and approval in the district. I mean, in the regional office.

asr-005094
04:09:59.340 --> 04:10:09.960
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: And I would like you to revisit it because, you know, for people who has less resources, cannot follow up in the Manila office. Cannot follow up.

asr-005100
04:10:10.680 --> 04:10:17.300
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: I talked with someone, they say it can be had by Zoom, by email.

asr-005103
04:10:17.620 --> 04:10:24.940
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: But, you know, if you go to the powerpoint, there's no email there. There's no facility for email. And so,

asr-005107
04:10:25.430 --> 04:10:33.960
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: I want you to revisit. I think it is DAO, it was approved last year, but then the previous one was several years ago.

asr-005112
04:10:34.420 --> 04:10:37.400
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: The one that was changed by Secretary Loizaga.

asr-005114
04:10:38.300 --> 04:10:44.460
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: And Loizaga asked that it be transferred to his office. Approval. Of all contracts,

asr-005117
04:10:45.700 --> 04:10:49.900
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: IFMA, CBFM, so, it's very taxing, Secretary.

asr-005120
04:10:50.240 --> 04:10:54.240
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: It would be a good legacy for you to have this.

asr-005122
04:10:54.760 --> 04:11:03.480
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: And we will, promote the stewardship for the meantime, and the processing for the poor people can do it.

asr-005127
04:11:04.480 --> 04:11:06.940
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: So, that is my last question.

asr-005129
04:11:07.200 --> 04:11:21.740
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you very much for your suggestion, Mr. Chair. Actually, what we can revisit, Mr. Chair, is probably to come up with some thresholds, depending on the size of the application.

asr-005136
04:11:22.560 --> 04:11:32.920
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because, right now, all 25-year tenorial instruments are in the central office, but it doesn't even have to go up to the Secretary.

asr-005142
04:11:34.000 --> 04:12:02.220
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, yung mga 25 years na instruments are signed, the signatory is the supervising undersecretary for the particular bureau where the instrument comes from. For the Forest Management Bureau, undersecretary Leones, for the Biodiversity Management Bureau and Land Management Bureau, it will be Undersecretary Adobo being the supervising undersecretaries. But, we share

asr-005156
04:12:02.220 --> 04:12:14.000
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: your concern, Mr. Chair, that we will revisit yung thresholds kasi, tama, yung iba, baka kailangan sa region mag-file. Mr. Chair.

asr-005162
04:12:14.680 --> 04:12:31.420
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: With that, Chairman, I terminate my interpellation and again, in due time, we will move for the inclusion of that 400 million to the added budget. For DNR. And with your help, with your letter, we are going to push for it.

asr-005171
04:12:31.700 --> 04:12:33.200
Rep. Maximo B. Rodriguez Jr.: Mabuhay ang DNR. Good afternoon.

asr-005171-split-1
04:12:33.400 --> 04:12:34.480
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you. Thank you very much.

