Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So.

asr-006015
04:48:45.660 --> 04:48:47.040
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: White clay yan eh.

asr-006015-split-1
04:48:47.100 --> 04:48:48.720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: White clay. Naging brown na.

asr-006016
04:48:49.540 --> 04:48:52.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So is this considered small-scale or large-scale?

asr-006017
04:48:53.020 --> 04:48:53.760
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: White clay.

asr-006018
04:48:53.760 --> 04:48:57.240
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: The permit that was issued then by MGP.

asr-006019
04:48:57.320 --> 04:48:59.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, I know the permit. Yung itsura niya po.

asr-006020
04:49:00.140 --> 04:49:04.220
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: Well, it looks like large-scale to me.

asr-006021
04:49:04.260 --> 04:49:06.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. Thank you for your honesty.

asr-006022
04:49:07.830 --> 04:49:09.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: What are the DNRs?

asr-006023
04:49:09.540 --> 04:49:13.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: roles and responsibilities in relation to quarrying?

asr-006024
04:49:14.620 --> 04:49:19.260
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: In relation to quarry, we are the head of the Provincial Mining Regulatory Board.

asr-006025
04:49:20.660 --> 04:49:24.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. And what is the process also of confiscation of quarrying resources?

asr-006026
04:49:26.300 --> 04:49:27.860
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: I beg your...

asr-006027
04:49:27.860 --> 04:49:31.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: What is the process for the confiscation of quarry resources?

asr-006028
04:49:32.220 --> 04:49:36.420
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: The basis if there is proof that there has been an illegal act,

asr-006029
04:49:36.420 --> 04:49:45.360
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: of extracting the resources, then that can be seized and later confiscated by government.

asr-006032
04:49:49.940 --> 04:50:00.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And, sir, how does DENR treat remaining stockpiles of quarrying resources extracted by private entities with permits

asr-006033
04:50:00.180 --> 04:50:03.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: after the expiration and non-renewal of such permits?

asr-006034
04:50:03.940 --> 04:50:11.360
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: They were allowed, Your Honor, Mr. Chair, to be commercially disposed until...

asr-006035
04:50:11.360 --> 04:50:21.920
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: through two department administrative orders allowing them to dispose of the residual stockpiles.

asr-006036
04:50:21.920 --> 04:50:31.360
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: In this case, the former permittee has not availed of that provision of the DAO,

asr-006037
04:50:31.360 --> 04:50:37.720
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: and therefore we have disallowed the disposal of these white clay deposits inside the scope

asr-006038
04:50:37.720 --> 04:50:40.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero sino dapat po ang magdi-dispose nito?

asr-006039
04:50:40.520 --> 04:50:43.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Is it the provincial government? Is it the national government?

asr-006041
04:50:44.180 --> 04:50:53.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So what's the process?

asr-006042
04:50:53.940 --> 04:51:00.620
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: If it is the permit issued by the national government, then it is the national government which should dispose that. If it is a permit coming from the local government, then it is the local government which should dispose that.

asr-006043
04:51:00.780 --> 04:51:01.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-006044
04:51:01.680 --> 04:51:02.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because there are reports,

asr-006045
04:51:04.100 --> 04:51:06.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I think, alam niyo naman po ito, R.D.

asr-006047
04:51:06.880 --> 04:51:15.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: There are forcible entries in the quarrying mining area of APCC mining and hauling of white clay from the stockpile they're in

asr-006048
04:51:16.980 --> 04:51:19.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: by members of the Sagip Kalikasan.

asr-006049
04:51:19.240 --> 04:51:27.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: When I say Sagip Kalikasan, sila po yung mga, actually, yung alam ko, task force ng provincial government to collect taxes.

asr-006050
04:51:27.920 --> 04:51:28.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's what I know.

asr-006052
04:51:29.460 --> 04:51:34.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And other unidentified individuals.

asr-006055
04:51:35.020 --> 04:51:40.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And there are also reports na yung mga truck ay truck po ng Kapitolyo.

asr-006056
04:51:42.040 --> 04:51:43.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi po sa inyo.

asr-006057
04:51:43.160 --> 04:51:44.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Are you aware of it?

asr-006058
04:51:46.400 --> 04:51:54.500
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: We are aware of two truckloads that went to the site just this year, July.

asr-006059
04:51:55.120 --> 04:51:55.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-006060
04:51:56.460 --> 04:52:00.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, Secretary, yung report sa inyong two, 90 po yun.

asr-006061
04:52:00.820 --> 04:52:01.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ganun na po kadami.

asr-006062
04:52:03.200 --> 04:52:05.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because I know, malayo po, no?

asr-006063
04:52:05.280 --> 04:52:09.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I'm just informing you of what's happening in Siroma.

asr-006064
04:52:10.169 --> 04:52:10.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-006065
04:52:10.860 --> 04:52:16.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung stockpile po ay kinukuha ng ibang tao, hindi mismo nung may-ari.

asr-006066
04:52:16.020 --> 04:52:20.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At alam ko, parang, I'm not so sure of the case.

asr-006067
04:52:20.620 --> 04:52:30.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But my point is here, did DNR authorize these entries and taking of stockpiles of that certain area?

asr-006068
04:52:31.120 --> 04:52:34.140
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: We did not authorize the taking of the stockpile.

asr-006069
04:52:34.800 --> 04:52:40.220
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: There was a permit issued by the provincial government outside of the Siroma area.

asr-006070
04:52:40.460 --> 04:52:41.240
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: It's in Tinambac.

asr-006071
04:52:42.240 --> 04:52:42.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-006072
04:52:42.920 --> 04:52:46.340
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: And then they were able to extract some materials there.

asr-006073
04:52:46.340 --> 04:52:54.260
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: And in 2025, our office investigated an illegal mining activity in Siroma.

asr-006074
04:52:54.260 --> 04:52:57.240
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: And we found out that that entity has been doing it.

asr-006075
04:52:57.600 --> 04:52:59.540
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: So we recommended to the governor.

asr-006076
04:52:59.660 --> 04:53:04.500
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: We issued a CDO and we recommended to the governor to cease the stockpile.

asr-006077
04:53:05.040 --> 04:53:08.720
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: Doon po ah, doon sa ginuha, doon sa Tinambac, not in Siroma.

asr-006078
04:53:09.140 --> 04:53:14.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, actually po, yung sa Tinambac and Siroma, ano po kasi yun eh. Magkalapit lang yun.

asr-006080
04:53:14.160 --> 04:53:19.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So actually, nung hinarang na po sa Siroma, gumawa sila ng bagong daan.

asr-006081
04:53:19.280 --> 04:53:20.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang labas mo, Tinambac na.

asr-006082
04:53:20.920 --> 04:53:23.240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So I know my place and thank you.

asr-006083
04:53:23.320 --> 04:53:25.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung Siroma and Tinambac, magkatabi lang po yun.

asr-006084
04:53:25.780 --> 04:53:26.240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sige.

asr-006085
04:53:27.120 --> 04:53:29.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And, sir, alam niyo ba ibig sabihin?

asr-006086
04:53:29.440 --> 04:53:30.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ng Sagip Kalikasan Task Force?

asr-006087
04:53:31.380 --> 04:53:41.140
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: I think that is environmental task force created by the province to protect the environmental...

asr-006088
04:53:41.140 --> 04:53:43.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So are they deputized?

asr-006089
04:53:43.700 --> 04:53:44.320
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: Yes, your honor.

asr-006090
04:53:44.700 --> 04:53:46.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can I have a copy of the...

asr-006091
04:53:46.540 --> 04:53:47.000
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: Yes, your honor.

asr-006092
04:53:47.400 --> 04:53:50.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pag nag-deputize po ba kayo as a whole or per person?

asr-006093
04:53:50.580 --> 04:53:51.220
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: Per person.

asr-006094
04:53:51.440 --> 04:53:51.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Per person.

asr-006095
04:53:52.000 --> 04:53:53.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can I have that copy?

asr-006096
04:53:53.780 --> 04:53:54.400
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: Yes, your honor.

asr-006097
04:53:54.520 --> 04:53:55.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Chair?

asr-006098
04:53:55.860 --> 04:53:56.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Deputization order.

asr-006099
04:53:56.960 --> 04:53:57.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Order.

asr-006100
04:53:57.520 --> 04:53:57.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Please produce.

asr-006101
04:53:58.460 --> 04:53:58.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

asr-006102
04:53:58.860 --> 04:53:59.360
MGB Region V Regional Director Guillermo A. Molina Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-006103
04:53:59.880 --> 04:54:00.280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Okay.

asr-006104
04:54:00.400 --> 04:54:01.420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Your time is up?

asr-006105
04:54:02.520 --> 04:54:04.380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Second round na lang po or...

asr-006106
04:54:04.380 --> 04:54:04.540
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Okay.

asr-006107
04:54:04.740 --> 04:54:05.140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sige.

asr-006108
04:54:05.900 --> 04:54:06.220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yeah.

asr-006109
04:54:06.540 --> 04:54:13.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because before I ano lang for the second round, I would like to seek the wisdom of the Secretary.

asr-006110
04:54:14.860 --> 04:54:16.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kaya hindi help us in Siroma.

asr-006111
04:54:17.260 --> 04:54:19.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ito pong white play na to, sobrang abuso na po ito.

asr-006112
04:54:20.400 --> 04:54:24.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, Secretary, I've warned RID and I've warned you.

asr-006113
04:54:25.180 --> 04:54:26.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Even the 19th Congress.

asr-006114
04:54:26.920 --> 04:54:27.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Fix this.

asr-006115
04:54:28.120 --> 04:54:30.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung nakita niyo po, small scale, it's large scale.

asr-006116
04:54:31.760 --> 04:54:33.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sobrang abuso na po ito.

asr-006117
04:54:33.940 --> 04:54:35.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sana po umahin ito.

asr-006118
04:54:35.160 --> 04:54:39.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Total ban of the white clay mining in Siroma.

asr-006119
04:54:39.440 --> 04:54:41.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I have to protect my district.

asr-006120
04:54:41.700 --> 04:54:44.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I have to protect the people of my district.

asr-006121
04:54:44.540 --> 04:54:45.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, sir.

asr-006122
04:54:45.900 --> 04:54:46.500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Okay.

asr-006123
04:54:46.540 --> 04:54:48.000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Thank you, Kong Ernie.

asr-006124
04:54:48.620 --> 04:54:51.240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: And next is Congressman Dumogan.

asr-006125
04:54:51.300 --> 04:54:52.000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Are you here? Sir...

asr-006127
04:54:52.360 --> 04:54:53.900
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Yes, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006128
04:54:54.500 --> 04:54:55.940
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006129
04:54:56.640 --> 04:55:02.980
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Good afternoon to the DEA and our family, hit by our good Secretary.

asr-006130
04:55:03.420 --> 04:55:12.240
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Of course, our regional officials of DEA in Kalkar who are also very competent and efficient

asr-006131
04:55:12.240 --> 04:55:15.660
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: in the performance of their function.

asr-006132
04:55:16.320 --> 04:55:24.380
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: First, Cordillera is one of the forested region entire the country.

asr-006133
04:55:24.800 --> 04:55:30.660
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: I was listening to your budget for intensified forest protection.

asr-006134
04:55:31.060 --> 04:55:39.660
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Is there a specific budget which are for the national park, forest water reserves?

asr-006135
04:55:39.660 --> 04:55:49.480
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Because, look, the sources of water that supply the dam going to Isabela is from mountain

asr-006136
04:55:49.480 --> 04:55:50.040
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: province.

asr-006137
04:55:50.400 --> 04:56:00.580
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: The sources of water that is this dam of Ambuklao, Binga, and San Roque also from Mountain Province.

asr-006139
04:56:00.940 --> 04:56:12.400
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Yet, it appears that we do not have the sufficient program to somewhat address the concern

asr-006140
04:56:12.400 --> 04:56:17.120
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: of the surrounding areas and to protect the forest reserve.

asr-006141
04:56:18.020 --> 04:56:20.540
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: So do we have a specific budget for that?

asr-006142
04:56:21.460 --> 04:56:23.080
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you for your question, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006143
04:56:23.160 --> 04:56:25.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We do have specific budgets for that.

asr-006144
04:56:25.120 --> 04:56:29.440
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: I'd like to defer to Yusek Anate for the details on this, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006145
04:56:29.440 --> 04:56:32.160
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

asr-006146
04:56:32.160 --> 04:56:33.960
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006147
04:56:33.960 --> 04:56:40.780
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Under the National Greening Program, Mr. Chairman, we have development activities within protection

asr-006148
04:56:40.780 --> 04:56:46.440
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: zone where we can undertake enrichment planting and assisted natural generation.

asr-006149
04:56:46.440 --> 04:56:51.560
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: For 2027, we have targeted 16,000 hectares.

asr-006150
04:56:51.560 --> 04:56:57.060
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: I mean, the unit cost is 16,000 per hectare.

asr-006151
04:56:57.060 --> 04:57:03.420
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So that's about 8,000 hectares or a budget of about 130 million, Mr. Chair.

asr-006152
04:57:03.580 --> 04:57:09.740
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: We also have a separate budget also within protection zone for reforestation.

asr-006153
04:57:10.760 --> 04:57:14.340
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Within production zone, we have budget for agroforestry.

asr-006154
04:57:14.340 --> 04:57:24.880
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: And for other areas that we mentioned, forest reserves, we do site planning and site protection and maintenance, Mr. Chair.

asr-006156
04:57:25.120 --> 04:57:31.080
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: And we also conduct support activities to provide technical assistance, Mr. Chair.

asr-006157
04:57:32.660 --> 04:57:34.160
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Madam.

asr-006158
04:57:36.500 --> 04:57:46.140
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: I hope that this is sufficient because if it is not, I'm one of those who are willing to move for an augmentation of that budget.

asr-006159
04:57:46.480 --> 04:57:48.140
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: For it is very necessary.

asr-006160
04:57:51.060 --> 04:57:58.840
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: On my next point, solid waste disposal system is a serious problem in entire the country.

asr-006161
04:57:59.840 --> 04:58:06.500
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: And one of the problem is the solid disposal site.

asr-006162
04:58:06.800 --> 04:58:13.920
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: It is DNR that actually disposes alienable and disposable public lands.

asr-006163
04:58:13.920 --> 04:58:20.680
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: But it appears that we have not reserved a solid waste disposal site.

asr-006164
04:58:21.740 --> 04:58:28.040
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: That's why in certain areas, you cannot locate an area for solid disposal site.

asr-006165
04:58:28.140 --> 04:58:29.020
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: So difficult.

asr-006166
04:58:30.120 --> 04:58:38.380
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Maybe it's not too late if we respectfully request DNR through the, I think, the Land Management Bureau

asr-006167
04:58:38.380 --> 04:58:50.020
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: to somewhat segregate suitable areas aside for solid waste disposal system.

asr-006168
04:58:50.560 --> 04:58:54.000
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Of our different provinces and cities.

asr-006169
04:58:54.900 --> 04:59:01.400
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: We experienced in the city of Baguio, we went to La Union to look for a site.

asr-006170
04:59:01.920 --> 04:59:04.840
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Even to Pangasinan, you cannot locate one.

asr-006171
04:59:05.120 --> 04:59:06.300
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: So it's so difficult.

asr-006172
04:59:06.940 --> 04:59:14.800
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: So I hope this will be taken seriously by the DNR.

asr-006173
04:59:20.840 --> 04:59:24.920
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Solid Waste Management, Environmental Management Bureau,

asr-006174
04:59:27.920 --> 04:59:29.160
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: What say you po?

asr-006175
04:59:31.600 --> 04:59:36.820
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Bakit na walang mga ma-designated managed solid waste disposal areas?

asr-006176
04:59:38.660 --> 04:59:40.780
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Sabi ni Congressman Dumugan.

asr-006177
04:59:40.900 --> 04:59:42.000
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Sa Baguio, wala.

asr-006178
04:59:42.040 --> 04:59:45.660
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Pumapunta pa sila sa Ilocos Norte para magdam ng garbage doon.

asr-006180
04:59:48.720 --> 04:59:49.040
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Yeah,

asr-006181
04:59:49.240 --> 04:59:51.780
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: is Kapas Disposal Site, pinupuntahan

asr-006182
04:59:51.780 --> 04:59:51.960
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: namin.

asr-006183
04:59:55.680 --> 04:59:56.900
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: Mr. Chair,

asr-006184
04:59:58.140 --> 05:00:00.440
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: meron po kasi tayong requirement under

asr-006185
05:00:00.440 --> 05:00:02.620
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: 9003 for siting

asr-006186
05:00:02.620 --> 05:00:04.360
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: criterias for sanitary landfill.

asr-006187
05:00:04.780 --> 05:00:05.420
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: And

asr-006188
05:00:05.420 --> 05:00:07.660
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: one of which, yung

asr-006189
05:00:07.660 --> 05:00:10.540
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: cars area, for example, sir, bawal po doon.

asr-006190
05:00:10.620 --> 05:00:11.680
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: And yung mga

asr-006191
05:00:12.680 --> 05:00:14.600
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: timberland protected areas

asr-006192
05:00:14.600 --> 05:00:16.100
EMB Director Michael Drake P. Matias: or yung mga near aquifers.

