asr-006976
05:30:28.620 --> 05:30:37.960
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Mr. Chair, we have allocated 278 million pesos for integrated water resource management and operations.

asr-006977
05:30:38.180 --> 05:30:44.380
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So that would include operationalization of the water resource management office and water-related projects.

asr-006978
05:30:44.700 --> 05:30:51.100
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: We're also supporting the water resource utilization section within our regional offices,

asr-006979
05:30:51.100 --> 05:30:57.120
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: although it's a minimal amount of 52.9 million pesos.

asr-006980
05:30:59.180 --> 05:31:09.100
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: But on the river basin, we're also providing support of 21 million for the sustainable operations.

asr-006981
05:31:09.740 --> 05:31:17.080
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So, and we have another 28 million for what Director Bill mentioned about scaling up nature-based solutions.

asr-006982
05:31:17.320 --> 05:31:19.320
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So, these are the sources.

asr-006982-split-1
05:31:19.740 --> 05:31:20.700
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Sasapat 'yan, ma'am?

asr-006983
05:31:20.800 --> 05:31:28.180
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Well, of course, it's not sufficient even in terms of really making sure the monitoring.

asr-006984
05:31:28.340 --> 05:31:31.300
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: But we will, we agree that we will prioritize.

asr-006985
05:31:31.680 --> 05:31:40.360
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: We have identified 18 principal or major river basins to... to focus on, Mr. Chair.

asr-006987
05:31:40.720 --> 05:31:51.840
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Okay, thank you, ma'am. Thank you, Mr. Chair. Another thing, sa Jensen, nung tumama yung magnitude 7.8 na lindol,

asr-006989
05:31:52.560 --> 05:31:57.260
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: napagalaman namin na a year before nangyari yun,

asr-006990
05:31:57.260 --> 05:32:07.160
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: nagsumite na ng report si PHIVOLCS sa LGU na kung saan merong 38% sa barangay ng GenSan may liquefaction.

asr-006991
05:32:08.880 --> 05:33:02.640
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Yung concern ko sa MGB, yung sa geohazard mapping, paano siya ma-merge or ma-integrate yung liquefaction? Kasi with our experience, pag nagbigay yung PHIVOLCS doon sa LGU, hindi nami-merge yung data sa geohazard mapping nila. Hindi naka-layer. So, magkaiba yung data na natatanggap at saka yung sa geohazard mapping. Ngayon, paano siya makaka-comply yung mga bagong building permits at saka yung zoning ng CLUP? Dadalawa yung basis nila. Mr. Secretary.

asr-007001
05:33:03.960 --> 05:33:05.820
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-007002
05:33:05.820 --> 05:33:10.280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We'd like to defer to Dr. Karlo. The assistant director of MGB.

asr-007004
05:33:11.460 --> 05:33:33.840
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Thank you, Secretary. I'd like to respond. As a geologist, we're implementing the Department Administrative Order 2000-28 in which all infrastructures, whether government or private, should conduct an engineering, geological, and geo-hazard assessment as an additional requirement for the issuance of the ECC.

asr-007010
05:33:34.160 --> 05:33:43.700
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, essentially, before you construct a building, you should know the physical conditions, if it's liquefaction-prone, if it's flood-prone, or maybe if it's landslide-prone.

asr-007013
05:33:43.780 --> 05:34:08.340
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, basically, you map out all of these geo-hazards. So, it's not just simply superimposing the liquefaction because liquefaction and volcanic-related hazards are the mandates of the Philippine Institute of Volcanology. But in the same way, identifying the faults, and that's also perform the fevals. But on the side of the MGB, DNR, that's flooding and landslide, as well as what we call the karst, and to a certain extent, coast.

asr-007019
05:34:08.660 --> 05:34:16.920
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: But regardless of the mandate, it is important in the DNR admissive order that all of these hazards are looked into by the private entity.

asr-007021
05:34:17.240 --> 05:34:37.940
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, the process is the private entity would hire a private geologist to produce an engineering, geological, and geo-hazard assessment, after which the DNR MGB would review that document as to whether the document is able to address this hazard and design a particular infrastructure according to the hazard.

asr-007026
05:34:38.080 --> 05:34:40.840
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, it's not just simply mitigating, but also adapting the structure.

asr-007027
05:34:40.840 --> 05:34:44.060
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Okay. Mr. Chair, yung concern lang,

asr-007028
05:34:44.060 --> 05:34:49.180
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: yung sa geo-hazard mapping ba ng DNR, kasama na ang liquefaction doon?

asr-007029
05:34:49.180 --> 05:34:51.440
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Hindi. Feebox yun?

asr-007030
05:34:51.640 --> 05:34:56.000
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Yes po. That's why po, in the geo-risk hazards hunter,

asr-007031
05:34:56.000 --> 05:35:01.160
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: these maps are integrated so that the end user would be able to make use of all of these maps po.

asr-007032
05:35:01.160 --> 05:35:33.040
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Hindi kasi yung concern namin, nalimbawa sa DPWH, yung sabi ng DPWH, hindi magkakaroon, nang future, kailangan may concordance ng DNR, yung mga future projects, especially related to flood control. Pero kung hindi nakasama yung liquefaction map doon sa basis ni DNR, possible pa rin na may mangyayaring masama kung sakaling may liquefaction na hindi siya na-factor in doon.

asr-007040
05:35:33.620 --> 05:35:40.740
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Tama po yan. That's why po, importante po sa isang building, or whatever infrastructure that these hazards are integrated,

asr-007042
05:35:41.160 --> 05:35:46.560
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: unfortunately po for Gensan, it is underlain, a large portion of it is underlain by Lahar.

asr-007044
05:35:46.820 --> 05:35:50.700
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: That's the reason why kapag naglindolo, matindi po yung ground shaking po niya.

asr-007045
05:35:50.940 --> 05:35:57.180
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: And also, liquefaction is one of those, what you call these consequences of strong ground shaking.

asr-007046
05:35:57.180 --> 05:36:02.700
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: That's why po, sa mga ganyang klaseng mga lugar, importante yung na-integrate yan sa design.

asr-007048
05:36:02.980 --> 05:36:08.400
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: I mean to say, yung liquefiable, for example, na layer, ay bina-bypass po ng foundation ng isang building mo.

asr-007050
05:36:08.500 --> 05:36:19.800
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: But I believe po, because of the DNR business order, that is actually a requirement for all these private entities to integrate all of these hazards before implementing that project po.

asr-007053
05:36:20.180 --> 05:36:26.120
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Mr. Chair, yung concern ko, Mr. Chair, kung may way ba na ma-merge yung data na yan,

asr-007054
05:36:30.860 --> 05:36:46.100
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: DNR, ma-merge yung data na yan para pag nagbigay ng certification or concurrency DNR, kasama na yun, na-consider na yung ano, kasama yung data, nang liquefaction.

asr-007057
05:36:46.320 --> 05:36:47.280
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: May I reply po?

asr-007058
05:36:47.500 --> 05:36:55.180
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Actually po, the municipalities at lahat po ng mga provincial, they can actually superimpose all of these maps.

asr-007060
05:36:55.180 --> 05:36:58.160
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Dahil lang po yan ay available po nga po sa Hazards Hunter.

asr-007061
05:36:58.480 --> 05:37:08.380
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: But of course, on the part of the DNR MGB, we are also offer our assistance to review all of the CLUP that also integrates this kind of hazard.

asr-007063
05:37:08.500 --> 05:37:16.460
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So as to be able to all these local governments to understand, and how to actually make use of those maps in the context of their land use plans.

asr-007065
05:37:17.580 --> 05:37:20.760
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Okay, that's all, Mr. Chair. Thank you.

asr-007066
05:37:21.000 --> 05:37:21.880
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Thank you very much.

asr-007067
05:37:22.420 --> 05:37:24.540
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Next on the list is Congresswoman Vergara.

asr-007068
05:37:25.180 --> 05:37:26.140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sir, you have the floor.

asr-007069
05:37:26.900 --> 05:37:28.080
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Maraming salamat po.

asr-007070
05:37:31.140 --> 05:37:33.780
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Sasagot lang po ako ng konti para sa inyo.

asr-007071
05:37:34.520 --> 05:37:37.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Matagal po ako nag-mayor ng Cabanatuan City.

asr-007072
05:37:38.320 --> 05:37:41.540
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Anyway po, talagang dapat, unfortunately,

asr-007073
05:37:42.060 --> 05:37:42.860
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: unfortunately,

asr-007074
05:37:43.120 --> 05:37:47.460
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: ang Pilipinas ay nasa ring of fire.

asr-007075
05:37:47.820 --> 05:37:53.300
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: At saka ang NSCP at saka mga building code natin,

asr-007076
05:37:53.360 --> 05:37:56.880
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: nakalagay na maliwanag na zone 4 tayo dapat.

asr-007077
05:37:56.920 --> 05:37:59.220
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Zone 4 tayo dapat.

asr-007078
05:38:00.260 --> 05:38:04.300
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, kaya po, kahit na dalawang palapag lang,

asr-007079
05:38:05.160 --> 05:38:09.000
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: talagang tine-check ng munisipyo o ng isang syudad,

asr-007080
05:38:09.780 --> 05:38:10.100
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: mabuti.

asr-007081
05:38:10.980 --> 05:38:16.180
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: And then, hihingi po tayo ng tulong sa nasyonal kung meron po silang datus.

asr-007083
05:38:19.140 --> 05:38:29.180
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ako po ay sumagot para sa inyo dahil yung mga pamangkimbo ko po ay Tiga General Santos, alam naman po nyo.

asr-007085
05:38:29.750 --> 05:38:34.340
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: At alam nyo, yung Jalibiron, nahulog.

asr-007086
05:38:34.360 --> 05:38:37.160
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Pero yung ospital nyo ang ginagawa, ayos.

asr-007087
05:38:37.920 --> 05:38:41.480
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Kasi yung structural nga po ang pinag-uusap.

asr-007088
05:38:42.390 --> 05:38:47.860
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Anyway, Mr. Secretary, si Chair,

asr-007089
05:38:47.860 --> 05:38:55.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: mag-upisa lang po ako sa isang sulat ng National Irrigation Administration.

asr-007090
05:39:06.360 --> 05:39:10.920
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, ito po ay galing sa pantamangandam.

asr-007091
05:39:14.320 --> 05:39:17.100
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang sinasabi po ay napakasimple.

asr-007092
05:39:17.860 --> 05:39:37.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang sinasabi po ay may delay ho sa 37,500 mahigit na hektarya kasama na ang tatlong bayan ng Tarlac dahil sa illegal quarrying doon sa amin.

asr-007095
05:39:37.280 --> 05:39:44.320
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: 37,657.83.

asr-007096
05:39:44.320 --> 05:39:48.040
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Duly signed by the engineer.

asr-007097
05:39:48.040 --> 05:39:52.240
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: And sumulat po ang ating administrator.

asr-007098
05:39:53.240 --> 05:39:56.560
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Sa lahat ng ahensyang concern.

asr-007099
05:39:56.560 --> 05:40:01.540
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Dahil po, talagang malaking concern po yan.

asr-007100
05:40:01.540 --> 05:40:24.780
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Noong Disyembre po, ay natigil yung 37,000 hektarya na covered ni ng mga distrito. Ni Kong Swansing. Ni Kong Coco Salvador.

asr-007104
05:40:26.860 --> 05:40:32.120
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: At dahil sa sobra ng illegal quarrying sa Nueva Ecija.

asr-007105
05:40:33.000 --> 05:40:41.000
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: 205 ang recorded na nag-quarry ron.

asr-007106
05:40:41.520 --> 05:40:47.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ngunit, pakikita ko lang sa iyo, sa inyo po, yung COA report.

asr-007107
05:40:49.260 --> 05:40:50.260
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: COA report po ito.

asr-007108
05:40:50.360 --> 05:40:52.800
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Gov.ph, 2022.

asr-007109
05:40:54.500 --> 05:40:59.540
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Tinan nyo po ang koleksyon ng tax on gravel sa Nueva Ecija.

asr-007110
05:40:59.880 --> 05:41:02.600
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: 400,935.

asr-007111
05:41:05.960 --> 05:41:12.400
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Tapos o, 2023, 1,034,880.

asr-007112
05:41:14.080 --> 05:41:25.300
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: This is a classic case of kapabayaan. Dahil ho kasi, tayo po ay bumabaha ngayon. Dahil sa iisang dahil.

asr-007115
05:41:25.980 --> 05:41:28.340
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Buhat doon sa Sierra Madre Mountain Range.

asr-007116
05:41:28.340 --> 05:41:30.760
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Hanggang doon sa Caraballo.

asr-007117
05:41:31.000 --> 05:41:34.260
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Nakukonekta roon sa Cordillera Mountain Range.

asr-007118
05:41:34.260 --> 05:41:36.760
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Lahat po ay kinalbo natin.

asr-007119
05:41:38.780 --> 05:41:40.220
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Wala ho tayong magagawa.

asr-007120
05:41:41.100 --> 05:41:44.200
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, may Philippine fault to sa Gabaldon.

asr-007121
05:41:46.080 --> 05:41:52.340
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: At ang sinasabi ko lamang po ay isang bagay.

asr-007122
05:41:52.400 --> 05:41:54.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Kailangan po natin na...

asr-007123
05:41:54.280 --> 05:42:05.100
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: ...inigay naman po sa ayos na mabuti itong issue na ito sa illegal quarrying pagdating ho sa Nueva Ecija.

asr-007124
05:42:06.340 --> 05:42:10.420
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang tagal na hong issue nito, wala pong nangyayari.

asr-007125
05:42:10.420 --> 05:42:33.800
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: From MGB to EMB to DENR. Matagal na pong issue ito. May ang komitee ng... ...nang... ...Philippine... ...nang... ...Kongreso sa Good Governance ay... ...inaimbestiga po ito, Mr. Chair, sa COA.

asr-007133
05:42:33.800 --> 05:42:37.980
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Wala pa rin pong nangyayari hanggang ngayon.

asr-007134
05:42:38.840 --> 05:42:49.500
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, tatanungin nyo kung paano nangyayari ho na bumabaha sa atin dito ho sa Metro Manila.

asr-007135
05:42:50.980 --> 05:42:52.780
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Papaliwanag ko, Engineer...

asr-007136
05:42:55.580 --> 05:42:57.700
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: ...Karlo Quiaño po, Geologist po.

asr-007137
05:42:57.720 --> 05:42:58.860
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Larry. Larry?

asr-007138
05:42:59.100 --> 05:43:02.580
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Hindi po. Carlo Quiaño po, Geologist po, Assistant Director.

asr-007139
05:43:02.580 --> 05:43:06.820
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Anyway, akala ko po, Engineer po kayo po sa Geologist.

asr-007140
05:43:07.700 --> 05:43:15.100
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Pero, sinasabi ko lang ho sa inyo. Bakit merong Manila Bay Cleanup Drive?

asr-007142
05:43:15.800 --> 05:43:16.480
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Bakit?

asr-007143
05:43:18.020 --> 05:43:22.600
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Alam po ba nyo kung saan nag-uumpisa ang kilometra?

asr-007144
05:43:24.520 --> 05:43:25.540
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Kilometer post?

asr-007145
05:43:26.720 --> 05:43:27.400
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Luneta.

asr-007146
05:43:28.100 --> 05:43:29.780
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Sabi po ng ating chairman.

asr-007147
05:43:30.040 --> 05:43:31.620
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Dama po ang ating chairman.

asr-007148
05:43:32.760 --> 05:43:37.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Saan ho nag-uumpisa ang meters above sea level?

asr-007149
05:43:40.520 --> 05:43:48.740
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Saan ho pinagkunan? Nung mga iniiniyero natin kung saan ang meter above sea level.

asr-007151
05:43:48.740 --> 05:43:54.420
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Pagkatapos, isisising lahat sa ating Pangulo yung nangyayari.

asr-007153
05:43:57.860 --> 05:44:05.460
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: What is the basis for ascertaining the above the sea level?

asr-007154
05:44:06.200 --> 05:44:07.240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saan galing?

asr-007155
05:44:07.820 --> 05:44:08.520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saan ho?

asr-007156
05:44:08.720 --> 05:44:11.480
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saan ang measurement site ng sea level?

asr-007157
05:44:11.660 --> 05:44:13.320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Lowest point in Metro Manila?

asr-007158
05:44:14.040 --> 05:44:16.900
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: City in Manila or in Bataan?

asr-007159
05:44:18.100 --> 05:44:19.240
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ako na ho sasagot.

asr-007160
05:44:19.720 --> 05:44:20.660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sagutin mo na po.

asr-007161
05:44:21.800 --> 05:44:22.440
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Okay.

asr-007162
05:44:22.680 --> 05:44:23.480
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi nila kaya.

asr-007163
05:44:23.480 --> 05:44:24.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Bigayin mo yung ano.

asr-007164
05:44:24.920 --> 05:44:27.240
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ito yung standard lang ito sa engineering.

asr-007165
05:44:27.480 --> 05:44:27.680
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Okay.

asr-007167
05:44:28.780 --> 05:44:29.480
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ayan na.

asr-007168
05:44:30.600 --> 05:44:31.440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Manood kayo.

asr-007169
05:44:32.320 --> 05:44:33.360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ganito po yun.

asr-007170
05:44:33.360 --> 05:44:34.880
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pinag-aralan na po ramin yan.

asr-007171
05:44:35.600 --> 05:44:46.200
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: From sa distrito ko po. Sierra Madre po kami. Distrito na. distrito ng 4th District of Nueva Ecija, 3rd District of Nueva Ecija,

asr-007176
05:44:47.360 --> 05:44:48.020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ilog yun.

asr-007176-split-1
05:44:48.040 --> 05:44:49.280
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: 1st and 2nd District,

asr-007177
05:44:50.140 --> 05:44:58.320
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: babagsak ho yan ang pinakamataas na bundok sa Sierra Madre sa Nueva Ecija ay Mount Kemalugong.

asr-007182
05:44:59.540 --> 05:45:01.960
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang pinakamataas na peak

asr-007183
05:45:01.960 --> 05:45:03.920
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: ay paa sa peak.

asr-007184
05:45:04.160 --> 05:45:07.980
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: 1,750 meters above sea level.

asr-007185
05:45:08.300 --> 05:45:09.320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Meters ah, meters.

asr-007186
05:45:09.580 --> 05:45:10.720
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Meters.

asr-007186-split-2
05:45:10.720 --> 05:45:11.860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saan galing yung measurement na yan?

asr-007187
05:45:11.880 --> 05:45:13.820
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, ano po ang mangyayari pag abong magyo?

